{"title":"Construct The Rectangle","difficulty":"Easy","statement":"A web developer needs to know how to design a web page's size. So, given a specific rectangular web page’s area, your job by now is to design a rectangular web page, whose length L and width W satisfy the following requirements:\n\nThe area of the rectangular web page you designed must equal to the given target area.\nThe width W should not be larger than the length L, which means L >= W.\nThe difference between length L and width W should be as small as possible.\n\nReturn an array [L, W] where L and W are the length and width of the web page you designed in sequence.\n\n## Examples\n\n**Example 1:**\nInput:\n```text\narea = 4\n```\nOutput:\n```text\n[2,2]\n```\nExplanation: The target area is 4, and all the possible ways to construct it are [1,4], [2,2], [4,1]. \nBut according to requirement 2, [1,4] is illegal; according to requirement 3,  [4,1] is not optimal compared to [2,2]. So the length L is 2, and the width W is 2.\n\n**Example 2:**\nInput:\n```text\narea = 37\n```\nOutput:\n```text\n[37,1]\n```\n\n**Example 3:**\nInput:\n```text\narea = 122122\n```\nOutput:\n```text\n[427,286]\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 <= area <= 10^7\n","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def constructRectangle(self, area: int) -> List[int]:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().constructRectangle","parameters":[{"name":"area","type":"int"}],"returnType":"List[int]","tests":[{"input":[1],"expected":[1,1]},{"input":[10000000],"expected":[3200,3125]},{"input":[1009332],"expected":[1058,954]},{"input":[1024123],"expected":[3293,311]},{"input":[1024835],"expected":[1645,623]},{"input":[1026031],"expected":[1026031,1]},{"input":[1043417],"expected":[4679,223]},{"input":[1044529],"expected":[1044529,1]},{"input":[1044879],"expected":[31663,33]},{"input":[1055670],"expected":[1155,914]},{"input":[1056701],"expected":[22483,47]},{"input":[1071359],"expected":[1071359,1]},{"input":[1071835],"expected":[4561,235]},{"input"